9h5|a|To soak, steep, or boil, in lye or suds; -- a process in bleaching. ; To wash (clothes) in lye or suds, or, in later usage, by beating them on stones in running water. ; To break up or pulverize, as ores. ; To copulate, as bucks and does. ; To spring with quick plunging leaps, descending with the fore legs rigid and the head held as low down as possible; -- said of a vicious horse or mule. ; To subject to a mode of punishment which consists in tying the wrists together, passing the arms over the bent knees, and putting a stick across the arms and in the angle formed by the knees. ; To throw by bucking. See Buck, v. i., 2.	j:fgx,89,27;9nm,75,1;1p3s,70,6;8ll,60,4;9v7,52,4;1ykg,40,4;1adk,25,3;203m,19,1;1xqy,6,1;1kqj,6,3~fgx,89,27;1p3s,70,6;9v7,52,4;1ykg,40,4;8ll,60,4;1kqj,6,3;1adk,25,3;203m,19,1;9nm,75,1;1xqy,6,1	e:7yj,4,1~7yj,4,1
